{"id":"8f6dc4191c5f2e6c","group":"67","path":"67/67-thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity.md","title":"Distributivity over Existing Bounds","display":"thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity — Distributivity over Existing Bounds","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom","book_abbrev":"67","label":"67-thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity","aliases":["67-thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity"],"display":"thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity — Distributivity over Existing Bounds","depends_on":["[[67-df-degree-bounds]]","[[67-thm-interpretability-lattice]]"],"source_file":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)\\[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf","source_edition":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition","source_chapter":"7","source_label":"Theorem 7.6(a),(b)","source_printed_pages":[99,100],"source_pdf_pages":[110,111],"verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"source-statement-and-book-argument-read; auxiliary proof chain not independently reconstructed","eligible_as_verified_dependency":false},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"67"},{"key":"label","html":"67-thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67-thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-degree-infinitary-distributivity — Distributivity over Existing Bounds"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"511859971a231477\" href=\"?note=511859971a231477\" title=\"67-df-degree-bounds\">67-df-degree-bounds</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"4ff6c9f71377d6d7\" href=\"?note=4ff6c9f71377d6d7\" title=\"67-thm-interpretability-lattice\">67-thm-interpretability-lattice</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:\\Users\\lzy\\Documents\\BaiduSyncdisk\\calibre\\libgen.li[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 10] P (2855)[Lecture Notes in Logic, Band 1 - libgen.li.pdf"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_chapter","html":"7"},{"key":"source_label","html":"Theorem 7.6(a),(b)"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>99</span><span>100</span></div>"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>110</span><span>111</span></div>"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"source-statement-and-book-argument-read; auxiliary proof chain not independently reconstructed"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"false"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,D_T,\\leq_T\">\\(T,D_T,\\leq_T\\)</span> 及格运算 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\wedge_T,\\vee_T\">\\(\\wedge_T,\\vee_T\\)</span> 采用 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"4ff6c9f71377d6d7\" href=\"?note=4ff6c9f71377d6d7\" title=\"67-thm-interpretability-lattice\">67-thm-interpretability-lattice</a>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Sup}_T,\\mathrm{Inf}_T\">\\(\\mathrm{Sup}_T,\\mathrm{Inf}_T\\)</span> 按 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"511859971a231477\" href=\"?note=511859971a231477\" title=\"67-df-degree-bounds\">67-df-degree-bounds</a>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"G\\subseteq D_T\">\\(G\\subseteq D_T\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"b,c\\in D_T\">\\(b,c\\in D_T\\)</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall G\\subseteq D_T\\;\\forall b,c\\in D_T\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Sup}_T(G,c)\\to\\mathrm{Sup}_T(\\{a\\wedge_Tb:a\\in G\\},c\\wedge_Tb)\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall G\\subseteq D_T\\;\\forall b,c\\in D_T\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Sup}_T(G,c)\\to\\mathrm{Sup}_T(\\{a\\wedge_Tb:a\\in G\\},c\\wedge_Tb)\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall G\\subseteq D_T\\;\\forall b,c\\in D_T\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Inf}_T(G,c)\\to\\mathrm{Inf}_T(\\{a\\vee_Tb:a\\in G\\},c\\vee_Tb)\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall G\\subseteq D_T\\;\\forall b,c\\in D_T\\;\\left(\\mathrm{Inf}_T(G,c)\\to\\mathrm{Inf}_T(\\{a\\vee_Tb:a\\in G\\},c\\vee_Tb)\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>对应印刷99–100页/PDF110–111页定理6。用界关系式同时表达右侧界的存在及其值，保留左侧界存在这个关键条件；不把 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"D_T\">\\(D_T\\)</span> 误写成完备格。空集情形也成立：空上确界为底、空下确界为顶。</p>\n<p>已读来源证明：(a)用引理6把 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\\wedge b\\leq d\">\\(a\\wedge b\\leq d\\)</span> 换成每个有限一致性否定扩张上的解释关系，再应用 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c\">\\(c\\)</span> 的上确界性质；(b)用引理10作对偶的后果比较，再应用 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"c\">\\(c\\)</span> 的下确界性质。引理10还依赖第4章定理3的编码，完整上游证明链未独立重建。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-df-degree-bounds","status":"resolved","id":"511859971a231477","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-degree-bounds]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-thm-interpretability-lattice","status":"resolved","id":"4ff6c9f71377d6d7","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-thm-interpretability-lattice]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-thm-interpretability-lattice","status":"resolved","id":